From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:30:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 612/612] pinctrl: mediatek: mt6797: describe the MSDC1 pad fields

MT6797 pinctrl maps only mode, direction and data, so a board can't
set the microSD pads' pull, drive, input buffer or I/O thresholds; they
stay as the boot firmware left them. The vendor MMC driver programs all
of them, and changes drive and the input threshold for 1.8 V signalling.

Describe the fields of GPIO129-134 (MSDC1 CMD, DAT0-3, CLK) in IOCFG_B:
input enable at 0x020, TDSEL at 0x0c0, RDSEL at 0x0a0, drive at 0x1b0,
and PUPD/R0/R1 at 0x100/0x110/0x120. DAT0-3 share one drive, TDSEL and
RDSEL field. Drive uses the 2-16 mA scale of DRV_GRP4 through the rev1
callbacks, and pull uses the PUPD/R1/R0 combo callbacks. The separate
bias-tuning bits at 0x1b0 bits 16-20 are left alone.

Other pins keep their current unsupported behaviour.

The field map is from the vendor GPIO table and MMC pad definitions,
the same map as the earlier upstream-preparation topics against
7.3-rc1, here in one change for the 7.1.3 station series.

Not yet run on hardware.
